DESCRIPTION:Hi Tim\,\nPer my Teams message and your reply putting in a 3
 0 mins catchup.\n@David Barrow<mailto:david@itsmpeople.co.uk> I know you
  have limited time for NR so put you as optional.  I have put it just in
  front of our existing meet as if we finish early we can flow into the n
 ext one and free you up earlier from the 2pm one.\nI need some direction
  on protocol for delivering the SD&T recommendation report / deliverable
 s from the SOW.   I have a call with Tracey 3pm on Monday to discuss and
  agree but wanted your guidance.\nWhat is the usual sequence?\nDo they g
 et to review the deliverables and provide a one time feedback\, then get
  an updated one and that is updated and sent back and called "complete"?
 \nIt's looking like I have another contract to go to at the end of Octob
 er\, so I'm aiming to complete this NR assignment by then (ie do the 40 
 days and in that time issue the final report ).\nSo if that is the case\
 , do I need to work back and send a draft version first say a week befor
 e and schedule in 2 days with the client to review it and feedback so I 
 have time (and days left) to review it and send back before the 40 days 
 is up / end October? What is the way you have told the client? / what is
  the norm?\nTina\n\n\n__________________________________________________
