DESCRIPTION:Hello there\,\nPoor Mia is unwell\, so I figured I’d set thi
 s up to get the convo started. Hope it works for you?\nFrom: Tim Mills <
 tim@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nDate: Tuesday\, 21 October 2025 at 16:08\nTo: Tin
 a Davenport <tina@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nCc: David Barrow <david@itsmpeople.
 co.uk>\, Mia Marston <mia@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSubject: Re: NR / SDT revie
 w output - potential follow on / priority actions and recommendations\nH
 i Tina\,\n\nThanks for confirming. Understood on the 3rd Nov timing - ma
 kes sense to give them sufficient notice.\n\nMia will send a calendar in
 vite for us all to chat when David is back. Looking forward to catching 
 up and moving this forward.\n\nTim\n\n\nFrom: Tina Davenport <tina@itsmp
 eople.co.uk>\nDate: Tuesday\, 21 October 2025 15:45\nTo: Tim Mills <tim@
 itsmpeople.co.uk>\nCc: David Barrow <david@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSubject: R
 e: NR / SDT review output - potential follow on / priority actions and r
 ecommendations\nHiya\n\nYes\, that's fine\, I'm quite flexible this week
  as working on the reporting / documents.\n\nPer role due to start on 17
 th Nov\, but if I'm to let them down\, I would rather to it a couple of 
 weeks  before that as they have a hiring freeze from Dec (and don't allo
 w new starters during Dec) and want to give them chance to go to their 2
 nd choice person in time to get that signed off. So that would be 3rd No
 v.\n\nTina\n________________________________\nFrom: Tim Mills <tim@itsmp
 eople.co.uk>\nSent: 21 October 2025 13:43\nTo: Tina Davenport <tina@itsm
 people.co.uk>\nCc: David Barrow <david@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSubject: Re: N
 R / SDT review output - potential follow on / priority actions and recom
 mendations\n\n\nHey Tina\,\n\n\n\nSorry been a bit manic!\n\n\n\nDavid i
 s off today but maybe the 3 of us should review the below together and t
 hen take it to Tracey for discussion.\n\n\n\nCan you remind me intended 
 start date of perm role so we can try to nip this in the bud before then
 ?! 😊\n\n\n\nThanks!\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Tina Davenport <tina@itsmpeople.co
 .uk>\nDate: Tuesday\, 14 October 2025 at 15:51\nTo: Tim Mills <tim@itsmp
 eople.co.uk>\nCc: David Barrow <david@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSubject: Re: NR
  / SDT review output - potential follow on / priority actions and recomm
 endations\n\nAh yes\, gotcha.  Yes a 6 month split into 2 x 3 month woul
 d work.\n\nWe would have to think about how to slot in the work with Jen
 ny though.\n\n\n\nIf we were going over 6 month it would be like this\, 
 ish.\n\n\n\nArtefacts review / consolidate (this would be ongoing for th
 e 6 months)\n\nHard to put a timescale on it\, as depends on the updates
  required\, and their Knowledge Manager buy-in\,  Also I would get them 
 to do a lot of the grunt work\, with my guiding\, setting standards and 
 educating.\n\n1 day per week over the 6 months. Total 24 days\n\nReview 
 current artefacts and create library with a view to storing as Knowledge
  see below: (Data strategy)\n\n  *   Update based on value add / issues 
 found / consolidation / de-duplication / reporting requirements\n  *   W
 ork instructions for artefacts (I can guide team how to write these\, ge
 t them started and review them)\n\n\n\nKnowledge Base\n\nDependency on K
 M buy-in to the Knowledge Champion aspect and supporting this venture\n\
 n10 days\n\nWork with Knowledge Manager where to store SD&T KAs\n\n  *  
  Identify Knowledge champion/s\n  *   Educate team\n  *   Help define pr
 ocedures for managing SD&T artefacts as knowledge\n  *   Support creatio
 n of knowledge (knowledge plan)\n\n\n\nCSI\n\nNeed Tracey to get align w
 ith Philip to confirm doesn't go against any plans for CSI in ServiceNow
 .\n\n7days\n\nCreate a mini-policy for CSI\, process \, RACI\n\n(use as 
 means to educate on policy\, process\, RACI)\n\nUpdate CSI log to captur
 e additional info as recommended in report\n\nRun a couple of POC pilots
  through it\n\n\n\nLifecycle\n\nThis could merge with the work Jenny - 2
  days per week for 6 weeks - 12 days\n\nDocument SD&T requirements for D
 elivery Lifecycle to feed into PMO work aligning Telecoms and IT Ops lif
 ecycle\n\nImplement short term workaround with PMO for ELS and Design ar
 eas of lifecycle (As documented in my report)\n\n\n\nSD&T Vision / Missi
 on\n\n3 days\n\nCreate an SD&T Vision / Mission (or we may have one from
  my report)\n\nReview the SD&T policy (after mini policy exercise above)
  in line with the vision mission.\n\nDefine next steps that would be req
 uired to bring that policy to life\n\nCreate action plan (will be things
  like KPIs\, tooling\, other teams policy requirements\, governance laye
 r\, reporting\, CSI initiatives)\n\n\n\nRisk Management\n\nFor just this
  below\n\n5 days\n\nWork with Risk Management to implement a workaround 
 for SD&T Risks:\n\n  *   How SD&T raise and report on Risks/ issues in p
 roject and ELS and Prod - Implement RACI for how these are owned\, manag
 ed with a view to in future update scope of Risk Mgmt policy to include.
 \n  *   Educate on link between Risk and Known Errors with view to chang
 ing how accepted risks are managed\n\nUnsure where this would go tbh at 
 this point\, depends on appetite and capacity of Risk team and if we dec
 ide to document a workaround or not.\n\n\n\nTooling\, Data/Metrics\n\n10
  days\n\nUpdate of SAC and Pipeline with fields so can be better reporte
 d and post quality checks.\n\nWork with team in NR to get reporting / da
 shboards set up as best can as workaround\, until DPR in place.\n\n\n\nT
 -shirt Sizing\n\n5 days\n\nImplement with a view to getting more accurat
 e capacity understanding across the team\n\n\n\nAbove totals 76 days (15
  weeks) - 3 weeks into 2nd chunk of work.\n\n\n\nThen onto next phase. 4
 5 days\n\n\n\nTooling\n\n15 days (maybe more)\n\nDPR requirements / impl
 ementation\, could help with SD&T side of the design of this and moving 
 into the tool.\n\n  *   POC\n  *   Reporting from DPR\n\n\n\nKPI measure
 ments\n\n1 day per week bit less - 10 days\n\nHelp build and advise on t
 he process by which KPIs feed into policy\, governance\, CSI's\, actiona
 ble items\n\nSupporting decision out of KPI metrics - driving action pla
 ns\n\nReporting on how achieving the Vision / Mission\n\n\n\nQuality Sur
 vey / post project\n\n5 days\n\nDesign / implement CSAT Survey - Policy\
 , objectives\, communications\n\nFields in current tooling to capture po
 st project success information - build into KPIs\n\n\n\nEducation in the
  team / training / mentoring\n\n10 days\n\nUpskilling / mentoring\n\n\n\
 nAd-hoc / contingency\n\n5 days\n\n  *   Supporting CSI initiatives\n  *
    KPI input\n  *   Results of Surveys\n  *   Tooling workarounds\n  *  
  Ad-hoc other team engagements to explain / back up directives\n\n\n\n\n
 \nTina\n\n\n\n________________________________\n\nFrom: Tim Mills <tim@i
 tsmpeople.co.uk>\nSent: 14 October 2025 14:11\nTo: Tina Davenport <tina@
 itsmpeople.co.uk>\nCc: David Barrow <david@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSubject: R
 e: NR / SDT review output - potential follow on / priority actions and r
 ecommendations\n\n\n\nYep understood 😊\n\n\n\nI guess regardless of you
 r personal situation (which is clearly an important part of this! 😊) \,
  at this stage it’s about providing a resource/project profile for them 
 to sign up to.\n\n\n\nSo for example if we say to them we think there’s 
 6 months of work made up XYZ\, and split into two chunks of 3 month burs
 ts of activity. We then get them to sign up to that and then we can tran
 slate that back into a contract for you.\n\n\n\nSo would be good to get 
 your view as to what that might look like in terms of time needed agains
 t those things below\, i.e. KB\, CSI etc 😊\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Tina Da
 venport <tina@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nDate: Tuesday\, 14 October 2025 at 13:4
 7\nTo: Tim Mills <tim@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nCc: David Barrow <david@itsmpeo
 ple.co.uk>\nSubject: Re: NR / SDT review output - potential follow on / 
 priority actions and recommendations\n\nFor me\,  to decline the perm jo
 b offer\, I really need some security of 6 months.\n\nIf this is via thi
 s project alone\, or by combining 3 months worth of work for 2 projects\
 , e.g Jennys Lifecycle and Tracey SD&T I could work part time on each st
 retching both to 3 months worth of work over a 6 months period that coul
 d also work?\n\n\n\nTina\n\n\n\n________________________________\n\nFrom
 : Tim Mills <tim@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSent: 14 October 2025 11:26\nTo: Tin
 a Davenport <tina@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nCc: David Barrow <david@itsmpeople.
 co.uk>\nSubject: Re: NR / SDT review output - potential follow on / prio
 rity actions and recommendations\n\n\n\nThanks Tina\, this is really use
 ful.\n\n\n\nWhat would you suggest from a time perspective on this?\n\n\
 n\nWrap into one big SOW over 6 or more months\, or go 3 months at a tim
 e and word some of the tasks carefully to make sure it’s understood that
  those items wont be completed within the SOW? (the latter probably more
  palatable and easier to get agreement on!)\n\n\n\nFrom: Tina Davenport 
 <tina@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nDate: Monday\, 13 October 2025 at 15:28\nTo: Ti
 m Mills <tim@itsmpeople.co.uk>\, Tracey Walker <tracey.walker@networkrai
 l.co.uk>\nSubject: NR / SDT review output - potential follow on / priori
 ty actions and recommendations\n\nHi Tim/ Tracey\,\n\n\n\nI understand y
 ou spoke about potential for a first set of priority actions following t
 he SD and T review.\n\n\n\nI do still need to completed the report but I
  think I can provide a high-level set of bullets based on what is coming
  out and the highest priority / impacting areas.\n\n\n\nI also have the 
 week to review projects with the SD&T analysts but I think that might fe
 ed into these anyway but provide more "cause" information and more detai
 l.\n\n\n\nArtefacts review / consolidate (this would be ongoing for a fe
 w months)\n\nReview current artefacts and create library with a view to 
 storing as Knowledge see below: (Data strategy)\n\n  *   Update based on
  value add / issues found / consolidation / de-duplication / reporting r
 equirements\n  *   Work instructions for artefacts (I can guide team how
  to write these\, get them started and review them)\n\n\n\nKnowledge Bas
 e\n\nWork with Knowledge Manager where to store SD&T KAs\n\n  *   Identi
 fy Knowledge champion/s\n  *   Educate team\n  *   Help define procedure
 s for managing SD&T artefacts as knowledge\n  *   Support creation of kn
 owledge (knowledge plan)\n\n\n\nCSI\n\nCreate a mini-policy for CSI\, pr
 ocess \, RACI\n\n(use as means to educate on policy\, process\, RACI)\n\
 nUpdate CSI log to capture additional info as recommended in report\n\n\
 n\nLifecycle\n\nDocument SD&T requirements for Delivery Lifecycle to fee
 d into PMO work aligning Telecoms and IT Ops lifecycle\n\nImplement shor
 t term workaround with PMO for ELS and Design areas of lifecycle (As doc
 umented in my report)\n\n\n\nSD&T Vision / Mission -\n\nCreate an SD&T (
 or we may have one from my report)\n\nReview the SD&T policy (after mini
  policy exercise above) in line with the vision mission.\n\nDefine next 
 steps that would be required to bring that policy to life.\n\n\n\nWork w
 ith Risk Management to implement a workaround for SD&T Risks:\n\n  *   H
 ow SD&T raise and report on Risks/ issues in project and ELS and Prod - 
 Implement RACI for how these are owned\, managed with a view to in futur
