DESCRIPTION:Present the ppt as a practice - talk through report.\n\n____
 ____________________________\nFrom: Tim Mills <tim@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSe
 nt: Thursday\, October 23\, 2025 4:11:39 PM\nTo: Tina Davenport <tina@it
 smpeople.co.uk>\; David Barrow <david@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSubject: Re: Fi
 rst Draft - Network Rail SD&T Review outcomes / recommendations\n\n\nHi 
 Tina\,\n\n\n\nThanks for the update and Tracey’s feedback - sounds posit
 ive. Glad those sections landed well\, and agree on keeping the tooling 
 detail and hierarchy slide given her preferences.\n\n\n\nMonday works fo
 r me - 12:15–2pm if that suits\, or tomorrow 9:30–10am / 1:30–2pm. If no
 ne of those fit\, feel free to use my scheduling link<https://meetings-e
 u1.hubspot.com/tim-mills>.\n\n\n\nLet me know what works.\n\n\n\nTim\n\n
 \n\n\n\nFrom: Tina Davenport <tina@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nDate: Thursday\, 2
 3 October 2025 16:11\nTo: Tim Mills <tim@itsmpeople.co.uk>\, David Barro
 w <david@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSubject: Re: First Draft - Network Rail SD&T
  Review outcomes / recommendations\n\nHiya\,\n\n\n\nI had a first quick 
 skim through with Tracey just now\, around size\, structure\, headings\,
  key power phrases I'd put in exec statements etc and the PowerPoint.\n\
 nWe did "fall out" briefly about the decomm of MS Project but then she g
 ot where I was coming from and told me she hadn't fallen out with me any
 more about it and agreed with me.  LOL. It's the problem with isolating 
 one small part of the report without the context of "all of it".\n\n\n\n
 She wants the tooling section of the word doc kept in (as you say justif
 ication\, she thinks tooling is really holding them back and this will r
 eally help)\, wants that kept in the slides as well. She said she can al
 ways hide those slides if needs be.\n\nSame with the What is SD&T\, she 
 liked those slides (well she used the word "love"! \, and the document h
 ierarchy slide she really loves (!) I think she is a visual person .... 
 she says that is pivotal to all of it so keep it in.\n\n\n\nShall I put 
 in something for Monday to go through it? (@David Barrow<mailto:david@it
 smpeople.co.uk> you don't work Fridays?)\n\n\n\nTina\n\n\n\n\n\n________
 ________________________\n\nFrom: Tim Mills <tim@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSent
 : 23 October 2025 15:54\nTo: Tina Davenport <tina@itsmpeople.co.uk>\; Da
 vid Barrow <david@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSubject: First Draft - Network Rail
  SD&T Review outcomes / recommendations\n\n\n\nHi Tina\,\n\n\n\nThanks f
 or these.\n\n\n\nTooling - agree it’s better in the main report for now\
 , given Tracey’s business case angle. If she wants a cut-down or appendi
 x version later\, we can easily adapt.\n\n\n\nPresentation - happy with 
 your logic. Let’s keep the “What is SD&T” content unless Tracey wants it
  trimmed\, as it helps her with internal positioning. Policy doc hierarc
 hy can move to appendix if space is tight\, but let’s see what feedback 
 she gives after today’s call.\n\n\n\nLet’s review any further feedback f
 rom her before making major edits.\n\n\n\nThanks\,\n\n\n\nTim\n\n\n\n\n\
 nFrom: Tina Davenport <tina@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nDate: Thursday\, 23 Octob
 er 2025 14:24\nTo: David Barrow <david@itsmpeople.co.uk>\, Tim Mills <ti
 m@itsmpeople.co.uk>\nSubject: First Draft - Network Rail SD&T Review out
 comes / recommendations\n\nHi both\,\n\n\n\nHere is my first draft of th
 e recommendations report.\n\n\n\nYou will see the Tooling section I've c
 onsidered taking it out as a separate doc or add as an appendix\, but Tr
 acey did originally say she thinks it would be best in the main report b
 ecause she wants to make a business case internally to expedite DPR for 
 her team\,  hence the level of detail here and in the ppt. I can run it 
 past her later today as I have a call with her.\n\n\n\nThe ppt\, I could
  shorten by taking out the section header slides and perhaps a tooling s
 lide and one of the what is SD&T potentially but again\, Tracey couldn't
  really tell me who she would present anything to\, if anyone. She did s
 ay she would appreciate some slides about what is SD&T to help her with 
 internal comms\, so hence I put them in.  I could remove the policy doc 
 hierarchy slide\, or put it in the appendix.\n\n​​​​\n\nLet me know what
  you think.\n\n\n\nI'll send you the other docs that are referenced\, in
  a separate email so it doesn't get confusing.\n\n\n\nTina\n\n\n\nTina D
 avenport | ITSM Consultant | www.itsmpeople.co.uk<http://www.itsmpeople.
 co.uk/>\n\n_____________________________________________________________
